1. Preface

ACP-Strip is public domain, meaning that you can use and spread the
program as long the archive contents stay unchanged. 
Archive contents must be:

 ACP-Strip                     10940 Bytes
 ACP-Strip.c                    2088 Bytes
 ACP-Strip.doc                  1873 Bytes

Minimum archive size must be    9102 Bytes

You are using ACP-Strip on your own risk. I cannot be held responsible
for any damage caused by ACP-Strip. This includes system crashes, bugs
in the program or this documentation.

2. The purpose of this program...

...is to strip logiles, or even other textfiles.

ACP-Strip has one special feature: It won't cut the lines in the middle, so
the stripped length will never reach the User-input exactly.

3. Installation:

Simply copy ACP-Strip to C:, or somewhere else you like.

4. How to use:

Start ACP-Strip without without any options, it's selfexplaining.

--------------------------------------------------
ACP-Strip V1.0  (C)1995 by ACP-Development

Usage: ACP-Strip <filename> <length>
--------------------------------------------------

Further you can use ACP-Strip with Cron-Programs like Event! or TPTCron.

5. Bugs

None known.

